> Martin, you've found a Magic Memory Vault (MMV). They contain a large
> sum of zorkmids, and are a good way to increase your finances.
> However, as you've found out, spending too much time in a vault will
> summon a vault guard, which are reasonably strong enemies.
> 
> Most players will use a pickaxe to break into vaults, particularly for
> use in getting divine protection from priests. However, it's possible
> to enter a vault in two other ways: teleportation from regular
> sources, and by activating a vault teleporter (resembles a
> teleportation trap, but gives you a message when you stand on it and
> hit ^T). Either of these ways will be bad for you, unless you can
> teleport out again.
> 

(mild spoilers:)
Also look for graffiti that says ad aerarium and search for secret
doors next to that spot.  The graffiti indicates that there's a closet
with a teleporter to the vault.  Use the teleporter and wait for the
guard to let you out of the vault.  Then when you come back with a
pickaxe, you already know where it is and you don't have to search.
Drop your gold before going into the teleporter; the guard doesn't
know the difference between your gold and the vault's.

Also, if you hear the footsteps of a guard on patrol, or someone
counting money, it means there's a vault somewhere on that level.



